---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer — Business Lab"
  description="Business Lab is educational only. It does not provide financial, legal, or tax advice."
  path=""
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container column prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Business Lab is for learning. It is not financial, legal, or tax advice.
      </p>

      <h2>What that means in practice</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Nothing here tells you what to buy, sell, or hold. No named funds, shares, or
          cryptocurrencies are recommended.
        </li>
        <li>
          No returns are promised. Where a lesson or calculator uses a rate, it is an
          illustration you typed or an example — not a forecast.
        </li>
        <li>
          The calculators show the result of the numbers you enter. They do not know your
          situation, and a result is not a recommendation to go ahead.
        </li>
        <li>
          Where a lesson shows market data it is at least 30 days old — the rule India's
          securities regulator sets for educational material — and it is never a hint about what
          happens next.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Rules differ where you live</h2>
      <p>
        Tax, business registration, and what counts as legal work for someone under 18 vary
        by country and sometimes by state. Lessons point to the official source for your
        country rather than guessing on your behalf. Check there before acting.
      </p>

      <h2>When to ask a person</h2>
      <p>
        For a decision that involves real money, debt, or anything legally binding, talk to
        a qualified professional, or an adult you trust, before committing. Business Lab exists
        so those conversations start from a better base, not to replace them.
      </p>

      <h2>Mistakes</h2>
      <p>
        Lessons are checked against their sources and carry a last-reviewed date, but errors
        happen and things change. If you spot something wrong, say so and it gets fixed.
        See <a href={`${base}/about`}>About</a> for how to get in touch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  li { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
</style>
